      "cooked": "<p>Jo man, don’t know if you can code, but take a look at my consignment_store app code. It shows how to quickly generate QRCodes using python.</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox githubblob\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/0x01d/erpnext_consignment_store/blob/develop/consignment_store/utils/qr_generator.py\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/0x01d/erpnext_consignment_store/blob/develop/consignment_store/utils/qr_generator.py\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">github.com/0x01d/erpnext_consignment_store</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <h4><a href=\"https://github.com/0x01d/erpnext_consignment_store/blob/develop/consignment_store/utils/qr_generator.py\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">consignment_store/utils/qr_generator.py</a></h4>\n\n<div class=\"git-blob-info\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/0x01d/erpnext_consignment_store/blob/develop/consignment_store/utils/qr_generator.py\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"><code>develop</code></a>\n</div>\n\n\n      <pre><code class=\"lang-py\"># consignment_store/utils/qr_generator.py\nimport frappe\nimport qrcode\nimport io\nimport base64\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nclass QRGenerator:\n    def generate_qr_for_item(self, doc, method=None):\n        \"\"\"Generate QR code when item is created\"\"\"\n        if not doc.is_consignment:\n            return\n\n        # Generate QR data\n        qr_data = doc.consignment_code\n\n        # Create QR code\n        qr = qrcode.QRCode(version=1, box_size=10, border=2)\n        qr.add_data(qr_data)\n        qr.make(fit=True)\n</code></pre>\n\n\n\n  This file has been truncated. <a href=\"https://github.com/0x01d/erpnext_consignment_store/blob/develop/consignment_store/utils/qr_generator.py\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">show original</a>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>Consignemnt is a custom type of Doc I have. qr_data can be anything.</p>\n<p>This is a custom app though, I haven’t looked into scripts or nocode yet. But someone else may be able to chime in… There should be some built in functionality to do this easily.</p>",
